  x-verified = {Verified 2026-09-23 through Crossref (author Cruz, R.L.; IEEE Transactions on Information Theory 37(1):114--131, 1991; DOI resolves; Crossref prints the title as "A calculus for network delay. I. Network elements in isolation", the journal's running head is "Calculus for network delay, Pt. I: Network elements in isolation"). Read in full text from a scan of the printed article (18 pages, running heads with page numbers 114--131). Section II, p. 116: a stream R satisfies the (sigma, rho) burstiness constraint if the data it carries in any interval [x, y] is at most sigma + rho (y - x); Fig. 2 and the text beside it identify the least such sigma with the largest backlog of a work-conserving system that serves at rate rho, which is the sigma of the proposition with rho = k. Eq. (2.3), p. 116: with packets of length L on a link of capacity C, sigma >= L (1 - rho/C). The article treats single-server network elements only; it has no multiserver element and no (k-1)L term. Given name expanded from the initials R.L. as the IEEE author record spells it (Rene L. Cruz)}
